From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reilly Brogan <reilly@reillybrogan.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Do not pin the OpenJPH version

OpenEXR pins OpenJPH to the same minor version, which prevents the build
from finding the system OpenJPH 0.33.0 and silently vendors an older copy
instead. Relax the version so the system library is used.

Origin: Arch Linux
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-08
---
 cmake/OpenEXRSetup.cmake | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/OpenEXRSetup.cmake b/cmake/OpenEXRSetup.cmake
index 9d7ee1e..a02de4e 100644
--- a/cmake/OpenEXRSetup.cmake
+++ b/cmake/OpenEXRSetup.cmake
@@ -272,7 +272,7 @@ set(OPENEXR_USE_INTERNAL_OPENJPH 0 CACHE INTERNAL
     "Whether OpenEXR bundles vendored OpenJPH into OpenEXRCore (0 or 1)")
 
 if (NOT OPENEXR_FORCE_INTERNAL_OPENJPH)
-  find_package(openjph 0.32.0 CONFIG QUIET)
+  find_package(openjph CONFIG QUIET)
   if(openjph_FOUND)
     message(STATUS "Using OpenJPH ${openjph_VERSION} from ${openjph_DIR}")
     set(EXR_OPENJPH_LIB openjph)
